   "evidence": "grep for `flip` in Decomposition.lean returns only line 28 (the docstring); `fromF1F2_isSymm` and `Bilin.flip_add_smul_of_isSymm_of_isAlt` have no occurrence in the file, and the repo-wide grep for `flip` under QFT/Scattering/DIS shows `flip_add_smul_of_isSymm_of_isAlt` used only by `lMuNuVA_flip` (Basic.lean:428).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Tensors/Decomposition.lean",
   "fix": "Add the lemmas the docstring points at, next to the other `fromF1F2_add_smul_*` characteristic lemmas: `fromF1F2_add_smul_flip (hSymm : g.IsSymm) (hA : A.IsAlt) : (fromF1F2 g K F1 F2 + c \u2022 A).flip = fromF1F2 g K F1 F2 - c \u2022 A` (immediate from `Bilin.flip_add_smul_of_isSymm_of_isAlt (fromF1F2_isSymm g K hSymm F1 F2) hA c`), plus the half-sum/half-difference forms mirroring `inv_two_smul_lMuNuVA_add_flip`/`_sub_flip`. Otherwise delete the claim from the docstring.",
   "issue": "The module docstring states \"The symmetric part comes out as the parity-even pair and the antisymmetric part as the parity-odd term (`Bilin.flip_add_smul_of_isSymm_of_isAlt` applied to `fromF1F2_isSymm`)\", but no declaration in the module says this: a reader looking for the hermiticity split finds nothing to apply. The parallel leptonic API exists in full (`lMuNuVA_flip`, `inv_two_smul_lMuNuVA_add_flip`, `inv_two_smul_lMuNuVA_sub_flip`), and ParityOdd.lean supplies only the antisymmetric half for a general `W` (`sub_flip_eq_div_smul`), so the hadronic counterpart is genuinely absent.",
   "line": 27
  }
 ],
